# Canvas conventions

- Use a single `#bracelet-canvas` with DPR scaling via `ResizeObserver`
- Split concerns: `layout.js` (math) → `render.js` (draw) → `engine.js` (input + loop)
- Layout consumes resolved beads `{ instanceId, product }`; never fetch Shopify here
- Bead visual size uses `size_mm` (tangent / cord) × `high_mm` (radial / face) via `mmToPx`; path radius is constant
- Cord occupancy always uses `diameterMm` (`size_mm`)
- **Pendants (`category` 吊墜)**: `size_mm` = bail/hook width on the cord only; `high_mm` = bail→tip height. Body hangs radially outward with **uniform** scale (aspect preserved) — never stretch to size×high. See `drawPendant` / `isPendant`
- Pendant hit box width stays narrow (hook-scale); hit-test picks the **closest** candidate so tall bodies do not steal neighbor taps
- **On-cord accessories (隔珠 / 字母 / 數字 / 星座)**: anisotropic stretch of opaque content to exact `size_mm` × `high_mm`. Placement connects by `size_mm`
- Round **beads** (`type: bead`): uniform scale into a circle (`highMm === diameterMm`)
- Track *represents* `max(sum(diameterMm), 130mm)` — ≤13cm locks to 13cm; above uses actual wrist
- Always scale placement angles to span a full `2π` so beads spread evenly (drawn size still uses true mm)
- Pointer events only (`pointerdown/move/up`); support touch on mobile
- Prefer filled circles only as fallback; prefer product PNGs from `/products/`
- Avoid requestAnimationFrame loops when idle — redraw on state/gesture/resize/image-load only
